### 13. DOM Heartbeat Indicator

A DOM element (not 3D) that pulses in sync with the phase's pulse rate:
```js
// CSS: #beat { width:6px; height:6px; border-radius:50%; transition:opacity 0.15s,transform 0.15s }
beatPhase += dt * PHASE.pulseSpeed * 2.2;
const beat = Math.pow(Math.max(0, Math.sin(beatPhase)), 6);
// ^ power-of-6 for sharp spike rather than smooth sine
el.style.opacity = 0.15 + beat * 0.55;
el.style.transform = `scale(${1 + beat * 0.6})`;
el.style.boxShadow = `0 0 ${beat * 18}px rgba(155,107,255,${beat * 0.4})`;
```
- `pow(sin, 6)` creates a sharp cardiac spike rather than smooth oscillation
- Phase pulse speeds: NREM=0.3, AWAKE=0.8, INSIGHT=1.0, REM=2.8

### 14. Orbit Control API Symmetry

When wrapping Three.js orbit state (`theta`, `phi`, `radius`) in a public `orbitCtrl` object, **all three must have matching get/set pairs**.

```js
// ❌ WRONG — phi and radius are plain properties; writes bypass the camera update
orbitCtrl = { updateCam,
  get theta() { return theta; set theta(v) { theta = v; updateCam(); } },
  radius, phi
};

// ✅ RIGHT — symmetric get/set on all three
orbitCtrl = { updateCam,
  get theta()  { return theta;  set theta(v)  { theta = v;  updateCam(); } },
  get phi()    { return phi;    set phi(v)    { phi = v;    updateCam(); } },
  get radius() { return radius; set radius(v) { radius = v; updateCam(); } }
};
```

**Root cause:** When only `theta` has a setter, any code writing `orbitCtrl.phi` or `orbitCtrl.radius` silently writes to a shadow property on the object, not the closure inside `updateCam()`. The camera matrix becomes stale until the next drag/scroll event — making the bug look non-deterministic.

**Fix pattern:** Clamp inside the `radius` setter, not at call sites: `radius = Math.max(8, Math.min(120, v))`.

Full note: `references/orbit-ctrl-symmetry.md`
